## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- ta-a row 1. The English “generally about 3 / 4 / 6 months” was already softened on purpose by R3. “சில தீர்ப்புகளில் … வழக்கமான அல்லது உத்தரவாதமான முடிவல்ல” is that rule, not a mistranslation of a usual sentence into an uncommon one. Restoring பொதுவாக would read as a typical sentence.
- ta-a row 4. Same advertising rule. “உண்மைகளும் சான்றுகளும் ஆதரிக்கும் இழப்பீடு” is the required wording. The suggested “அதிகபட்ச இழப்பீடு” is the maximum-compensation claim R3 removed.
- ta-a rows 10 and 11 are culturally right about “TWD 1.57M” looking like an English abbreviation and about lakh grouping. They are not applicable here: the bio figure is pinned, and the checker does not parse lakh/crore grouping. Part b of the same review already treats Western grouping as acceptable.
- ta-b row 29 is a real defect (U+200B, including lines whose only character is that space). It is not a wording mistake the fixer can remove: the block checker demands the same ZWSP count as the Korean source.
